it/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/deployments","created_at":"2018-02-01T11:46:10Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T02:15:59Z","pushed_at":"2025-02-03T09:50:22Z","git_url":"git://github.com/fastify/help.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:fastify/help.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/fastify/help.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/fastify/help","homepage":"https://fastify.dev","size":26,"stargazers_count":68,"watchers_count":68,"language":null,"has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":8,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":109,"license":null,"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":true,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":8,"open_issues":109,"watchers":68,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"#### What are you trying to achieve, or the steps to reproduce?\r\n\r\nEvaluating `fastify` in a few test set ups. Our use case scenarios are either `content-type: application/json` or `content-type: text/plain` which are supported by default. \r\n\r\nIt does appear though (please correct if wrong) that `fastify` _guesses_ the `content-type` of the response (based on the data type being returned) and automatically sets it, which can lead to incorrect results. I can override this in the `reply` object, but would have to do this in every handler method... \r\n\r\nexample 1: correct guess\r\n```\r\nasync handler(request: FastifyRequest, reply: FastifyReply)\r\n{\r\n  // `fastify` will guess correctly `content-type: text/plain`\r\n  reply.code(200).send('my text');\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nexample 2: incorrect guess\r\n```\r\nasync handler(request: FastifyRequest, reply: FastifyReply)\r\n{\r\n  // `fastify` guessed \"incorrectly\" `content-type: text/plain`\r\n  reply.code(200).send(JSON.stringify({foo: bar, bar: 'foo'}));\r\n\r\n  // hence will have to manually override\r\n  reply\r\n    .code(200)\r\n    .headers({'content-type': 'application/json'})\r\n    .send(JSON.stringify({foo: bar, bar: 'foo'}));\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI know that if just an object `{foo: bar, bar: 'foo'}` would be passed into `.send()` in example 2, it would then lead to the correct guess and setting of  `content-type: application/json`, but often data comes from other sources and is already correctly prepped or encoded, hence we know for example that we need `content-type: application/json`, no matter what `fastify` thinks.\r\n\r\nSo, is there a server config option that allows to specify a default response `content-type` that is then always used by `fastify` unless it is overridden by the reply object ?\r\n\r\n\r\n#### Context\r\n\r\n* *node version*: 14.6.0\r\n* *fastify version*: 3.20.2 \r\n* *os*: Win 10 x64\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/issues/517/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/help/issues/517/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":5232037243,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDUyMzIwMzcyNDM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/issues/events/5232037243","actor":{"login":"Krishanu230","id":7608868,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDg4Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7608868?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230","html_url":"https://github.com/Krishanu230","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krishanu230/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"refer